[{"text":"QuantumField is the head of quantized fields and their derivatives.","anchor":"quantumfield"},{"text":"QuantumField[par, ftype, {lorind}, {sunind}] denotes a quantum field of type ftype with (possible) Lorentz-indices lorind and \\(SU(N)\\) indices sunind. The optional first argument par denotes a partial derivative acting on the field.","anchor":"quantumfield"},{"text":"Overview, FeynRule, FCPartialD, ExpandPartialD.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"This denotes a scalar field.","anchor":"examples","section":"Examples"},{"text":"QuantumField[S]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[S\\]","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Quark fields","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"QuantumField[AntiQuarkField]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\psi }\\]","anchor":"cb2-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"QuantumField[QuarkField]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\psi\\]","anchor":"cb3-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"This is a field with a Lorentz index.","anchor":"cb3-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"QuantumField[B, {\\[Mu]}]","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[B_{\\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb4-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Color indices should be put after the Lorentz ones.","anchor":"cb4-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"QuantumField[GaugeField, {\\[Mu]}, {a}] // StandardForm (*QuantumField[GaugeField, LorentzIndex[\\[Mu]], SUNIndex[a]]*)","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\(A_{\\Delta}^a\\) is a short form for \\(\\Delta ^{mu } A_{mu }^a\\)","anchor":"cb5-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"QuantumField[A, {OPEDelta}, {a}]","anchor":"cb6","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[A_{\\Delta }^a\\]","anchor":"cb6-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"The first list of indices is usually interpreted as type LorentzIndex, except for OPEDelta, which gets converted to type Momentum.","anchor":"cb6-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"QuantumField[A, {OPEDelta}, {a}] // StandardForm (*QuantumField[A, Momentum[OPEDelta], SUNIndex[a]]*)","anchor":"cb7","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Derivatives of fields are denoted as follows.","anchor":"cb7-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"QuantumField[FCPartialD[LorentzIndex[\\[Mu]]], A, {\\[Mu]}]","anchor":"cb8","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left.(\\partial _{\\mu }A_{\\mu }\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb8-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"QuantumField[FCPartialD[OPEDelta], S]","anchor":"cb9","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left.(\\partial _{\\Delta }S\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb9-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"QuantumField[FCPartialD[OPEDelta], A, {OPEDelta}, {a}]","anchor":"cb10","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left.(\\partial _{\\Delta }A_{\\Delta }^a\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb10-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"QuantumField[FCPartialD[OPEDelta]^OPEm, A, {OPEDelta}, {a}]","anchor":"cb11","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\partial _{\\Delta }^m{}^{A\\Delta a}\\]","anchor":"cb11-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"QuantumField[QuantumField[A]] === QuantumField[A]","anchor":"cb12","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\text{True}\\]","anchor":"cb12-1","section":"Examples"}]